I'm not consistant about what I call the mid-game and what I
call the late-game.  For me it's mid-game until I have completed
both castles and the VotD, or until I have a complete ascension
kit of inventory items and spares in my stash.  I usually call
it the late game until I've taken out Vlad, found the VS and so
so.  I usually call it the end-game starting when I have all
the preparations and I enter Rodney's tower.

> The usual progress of things is: I get to the castle
> (without MR),

Lack of MR is definitely your problem, but it is not fatal.

> after ca. 10 turns an arch lich turns up, I run away from
> the castle.

If you're carefull, heavily armed, and remote, then killing any
L is doable.  Most of the attack wands hurt them, all missiles
hurt them, and you never want to face one in melee unless your
purpose is to get them to run up the stairs to a teleport-yes
level.

Without MR, when I see the Castle I use telepathy to count the
L's, then I go back to my stash to get every offensive wand and
missile I can carry.  Then I go to the drawbridge and use a
polearm on all trivial (non-magic-using) monsters.  Any time a
blast from a wand will hit an L, I zap away with utter abandon.
Eventually an L may come across the moat and then I'll zap and
throw and retreat.  L's are slow enough that remote attacks
often take them out.  Any L under arch-lich tend to not survive
to get off the bridge.  The problem comes in when they cast
summon-nasties.  Then you're in a crowd and your primary target
must remain the L.  On a teleport-no level like the Castle this
means you need a short path to the stairs dug before opening the
drawbridge, and you need to retreat steadily as an L advances.
I rarely hit the stairs before the L dies, but I still tend to
cycle up and down for a bit until the crowd thins.

With MR the story is very different.  I stand a square away
from the drawbridge taking out any monster that steps on it.
When an L appears I switch to zapping, casting, throwing until
it dies.  Then back to massacring mundane monsters until the
crowd thins.

If you ever come across a scroll of genocide, bless it and do
L first, problem solved in advance.  Definitely my favorite
method.  Genociding many types of monster makes the game
harder, but carefull selections like L, master mind flayer,
mind flayer, disenchanter do make the game easier.

